                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Full stop NO.  Upon trying to play this game after a very long hiatus, the latest build cannot handle either 2-screen setups or modern hardware.  Not sure which but I'm leaning towards the former.\n\nBefore the game fully loads, both screens misbehave, then black out.  The game finally appeared on my primary monitor w/ wrong resolution and at corner of screen.  Once the game loaded, it would not accept any input/controls.  Could not go into menu, options or anything.  Trying to initialize anything resulted in the game freaking out and both primary and secondary monitors blacking out before the game completely froze with audio playing in the background.\n\nCtrl-alt-del did nothing.  Alt-tab did nothing.  Only a hard reset.\n\nThere's likely a fix for this but I'm not wasting my time to correct the jank, especially not for a LEGO game whose series has been bulldozed into the ground in recent years by the \"modern\" Devs.\n\nWhen I could play this, years ago, I enjoyed it.  Simply unplayable now without the hassle of some fix.\n\nPC Specs:\n13700K @ 5.5 ghz\n64 gb DDR5 @ 6400mhz\n4090 MSI\nWin 11",
                        "timestamp_created": 1792704997,
